# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cherry-PIC — what stays out of the repository
#
# The analysis objects and hi-res panels are far past GitHub's limits (100 MB hard
# per file). Code, small inputs and small published panels are versioned here; the
# heavy artefacts are deposited separately and pointed to from README.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Analysis objects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seurat / AnnData / matrix formats. The largest single object is 5.8 GB.
*.RDS
*.rds
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.loom
*.mtx
*.mtx.gz
*.rda
*.RData

# ── Marker tables ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# wilcoxauc output. Raw tables run 400-660 MB, Filtered 13-27 MB. Both are
# regenerable from the objects and go in the deposit. The Top tables are small
# and stay in the repo.
*Raw-Markers.xlsx
*Filtered-Markers.xlsx


# ── Rendered figures ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every outputs/ directory. Visium HD panels carry the tissue image and run
# 40-240 MB each; even the "small" ones total hundreds of MB across the project.
# All rendered figures live in the deposit, listed in README.md. The code that
# makes them is versioned here, which is what a reader needs to reproduce them.
**/outputs/

# ── Manuscript figures ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The author's assembled figure PDFs — the manuscript, not the code.
Individual figures/

# ── Raw sequencing input ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/rawdata/

# ── Vendor delivery ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The original Biomni bundle, 1.9 GB of result tables and figures. Its SCRIPTS are
# kept (they produce Figures S5C-E and the 6F/6G/S8 analyses); the bulk data goes
# in the deposit. Directories are re-included first so the negations can apply.
Biomni-code-external/Full-data/**
!Biomni-code-external/Full-data/**/
!Biomni-code-external/Full-data/**/*.R
!Biomni-code-external/Full-data/**/*.py
# figure_legends.md documents how the LIANA and pathway panels were built and is worth
# keeping. The other 20 .md files in the bundle are the vendor's working analysis reports,
# including archived pre-run versions whose numbers were superseded — they belong in the
# deposit, not in a repository a reviewer reads.
!Biomni-code-external/Full-data/**/figure_legends.md

# ── Working scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sync scripts, dated backups and superseded documents. Local bookkeeping.
_sync/

# ── R / OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
.Rapp.history
Rplots.pdf
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Internal working notes — not for the public repository
PROJECT_NOTES.md

# Word lock files
~$*

# Manuscript documents — this repository is code only
*.docx
*.doc

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Biomni deliveries are kept as received; the corrected copies in
# Biomni-code-external/0*/scripts/ are the authoritative versions.
Biomni-code-external/Full-data/**/reproducible_package/**/scripts/

# Ligand-receptor scoring object (285 MB) - deposit with the processed data
Biomni-code-external/01_liana_nichenet/data/nichenet_obj.rds
